victron-energy-card
===================

This directory contains a modified copy of the dashboard card shipped with
"Victron VRM API for Home Assistant" by jayjojayson:

  Project:  https://github.com/jayjojayson/hass-victron-vrm-api
  Revision: main at 017c7dc0c6956c6602c5678f2b339a514257a1e1
            (installed card files of integration version 2.0, custom_components/victron_vrm_api/www/)
  License:  Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE in this directory)

The upstream frontend identifies Venus-OS-Dashboard-Card as its base.

Every JavaScript file here is derived from the upstream file of the same role
and carries a header naming its origin and stating that it was modified:

  upstream www/victron-vrm-api.js -> victron-energy-card.js
  upstream www/editor.js          -> editor.js
  upstream www/lib-venus.js       -> lib-venus.js
  upstream www/lib-editor.js      -> lib-editor.js
  upstream www/css-dark.js        -> css-dark.js
  upstream www/css-light.js       -> css-light.js
  upstream www/css-editor.js      -> css-editor.js
  upstream www/lang-en.js         -> lang-en.js
  upstream www/lang-de.js         -> lang-de.js
  upstream www/lang-fr.js         -> lang-fr.js

Substantive local modifications
-------------------------------

Identity and integration independence
  - Registered as custom:victron-energy-card with editor
    victron-energy-card-editor; not tied to the VRM integration.
  - Removed the VRM cloud coupling: sensor.vrm_* discovery, power/current
    heuristics in the stub config, the integration-provided resource URL and
    ?v= cache busting, the demo mode and the console banner.
  - One canonical getDefaultConfig() (the owner's Cerbo GX entities as
    published over MQTT: grid, battery, MultiPlus, loads; no solar box). It is
    used by getStubConfig() and by setConfig() whenever `devices` is absent. A
    configuration with `devices` is used as written.
  - Static ES module imports replace top-level-await dynamic imports;
    translations are imported statically.

Behaviour
  - New per-box `control_entity`: tapping a box opens Home Assistant's native
    more-info dialog (hass-more-info) for it instead of the reading. Boxes are
    keyboard-activatable. The card performs no service calls.
  - Missing, unknown and unavailable states render as "—" and are never read as
    zero; gauges empty for them.
  - Flows are driven only by a numeric link signal: missing, unavailable,
    non-numeric or |value| <= 0.5 (including zero) stop the flow and hide its
    ball. Links without a signal entity no longer animate permanently.
  - Consistent flow direction: positive values always move from `start`
    towards `end` (inv reverses). Upstream silently inverted links that join a
    side anchor (L/R) to a top/bottom anchor (T/B).
  - Flows are keyed per link, so several links from one anchor are independent.
  - Removed the animation self-recovery heuristics; the lifecycle (connect,
    disconnect, ResizeObserver) redraws instead.

Lifecycle
  - The card renders in its own shadow root; theme CSS no longer needs
    per-instance selector scoping (scopeCss removed).
  - History is private to each card instance: one batched recorder request
    for all graphed entities, a 15-minute interval that exists only while the
    card is connected, and a generation counter that discards responses after
    reset, reconfiguration or detachment. Shared global history caches and the
    retry-on-every-hass-update behaviour were removed.
  - A ResizeObserver redraws connection lines and auto font sizes on any size
    change, without waiting for a state change.

Safety and validation
  - All entity, config and state text is escaped for HTML text and attributes,
    including font sizes, link indexes, box keys and editor option labels.
  - Colours are restricted to plain colour syntax before entering CSS/SVG;
    font sizes to numbers or number+px/em/rem/%; ball size to (0, 20].
  - Box ids, anchors (1-3 per side, duplicates merged) and link geometry are
    validated; invalid entries are skipped instead of logged per update.

Editor
  - control_entity selector; secondary-value font size; unfiltered entity
    selectors for every field.
  - Entity and icon pickers write their value back so a hass refresh does not
    render a stale value; editor echo detection keeps focus.
  - Clearing a selector removes the key and an emptied `devices` mapping is
    kept, so defaults are never reintroduced.
  - Expanded-panel state is per editor instance.
  - Config edits own deep copies, including cleanup of empty mappings.

Styles
  - Compact container layout and minimum auto font sizes keep mobile values
    readable. The connection SVG scales to the card's dimensions.
  - Removed declarations without effect (invalid boxTitle font-size, z-index
    and box-shadow on SVG elements).
